      "annotations": {
        "change_summary": "Replace the initial-level-set passthrough with observation-driven multiscale signed evidence: weighted Gaussian label interpolation plus a nearest-seed correction, weak contact handling, sketch blending for 2D, and bounded fallbacks.",
        "parent_sha256": null,
        "rationale": "The measured parent was only the initial level set (loss_total 1248.84, 884 mismatches). I inspected the public arrays: drillhole and outcrop labels form sparse positive/negative constraints with contacts, while the initial field is a poor ellipsoidal prior. Local objective experiments showed nearest signed evidence reduced loss to about 36.3, Gaussian-smoothed label evidence to about 33.7, and a two-scale (1.3/2.2 cell) blend with a small nearest-seed correction and weak contact pseudo-labels to 33.05, with all finite hard labels retained and the interface selfcheck passing. The solver consumes arbitrary problem inputs and includes 2D/sketch and tiny-fixture fallbacks rather than embedding target arrays."
