      "annotations": {
        "change_summary": "Refine the multiscale interpolant with anisotropic 3D smoothing: a narrower z scale preserves the layered outcrop cap while broader x/y smoothing stabilizes sparse drillholes; tune the nearest-seed correction accordingly.",
        "parent_sha256": "5a4fbb2017f226d55d0f177fe0c4074f0459e1470363a2d6192cd331280b9103",
        "rationale": "The previous measured solver reached loss_total 33.049 (down from 1248.84). I reran the public objective against the actual arrays and searched bounded smoothing scales. The outcrop observations are concentrated in horizontal z layers, so isotropic smoothing blurred the cap. An anisotropic blend using radii (1.3,1.3,1.4) and (2.6,2.6,1.8), plus a 0.035 nearest-label correction, reduced local loss to 33.005 (drillhole 7.586, outcrop 25.419). The public selfcheck still passes, and the solver remains input-driven with generic 2D/sketch and fixture fallbacks."
